    <a class="card" href="/fitness-apps/best-fitness-apps-with-nutrition/"><h3>Best Fitness Apps with Nutrition Support</h3><p>What to compare when workout guidance and nutrition education are connected.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/fitness-apps/workout-videos/"><h3>Fitness Apps with Workout Videos</h3><p>How exercise demonstrations can support confidence, technique and consistency.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/training/"><h3>Strength Training App Guide</h3><p>What guided strength programming should include for beginners and experienced users.</p></a>
  </div>

  <div class="callout"><strong>Do not choose an app by feature count alone.</strong> A smaller system you can understand and repeat is usually more useful than dozens of disconnected tools.</div>

  <h2 id="ea">Where Everyone’s an Athlete is headed</h2>
  <p>Everyone’s an Athlete is being built around four connected pillars: <a href="/training/">training</a>, <a href="/recovery/">recovery</a>, <a href="/nutrition/">nutrition</a> and <a href="/mental-performance/">mental performance</a>. The goal is to make those areas easier to use together while keeping the experience approachable for people at different starting points.</p>
  <p>The app is still in development. In the meantime, the site’s guide library documents the approach, answers specific questions and provides practical movement education.</p>
